      <h1>Lumi – Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p class="updated">
        Effective Date: November 27, 2026<br>
        Website: https://lumi-56bs.onrender.com<br>
        Contact: little.labs16@gmail.com
      </p>

      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        Welcome to Lumi! Lumi is a study planning and productivity
        website that helps users organize tasks, build habits,
        manage notes, plan lessons, and track study sessions.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information Lumi collects,
        how it is used, where it is stored, and how users can manage
        or delete their information.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>When you create an account, Lumi collects:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Name:</strong> To identify your account.</li>
        <li><strong>Email address:</strong> To identify your account
          and support account-related communication.</li>
        <li><strong>Password:</strong> To authenticate your account.
          Passwords are hashed before being stored and are not
          stored as plain text.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>When you use Lumi, we also store information you provide through its features, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Tasks and their details.</li>
        <li>Notes and tags.</li>
        <li>Daily habits.</li>
        <li>Calendar entries and scheduled tasks.</li>
        <li>Lesson information.</li>
        <li>Study and focus-session settings.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>Lumi uses your information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Create and manage your account.</li>
        <li>Provide the website's productivity and study-planning features.</li>
        <li>Save and display your personal content.</li>
        <li>Authenticate users and protect accounts.</li>
        <li>Maintain and improve the website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Lumi does not sell your personal information or use
        advertising trackers.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Lumi uses an essential login cookie to keep users
        authenticated and allow them to access their accounts.
        This cookie is necessary for the website to function properly.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lumi does not currently use advertising cookies or
        visitor-tracking analytics tools.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data Storage and Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Lumi uses third-party infrastructure providers to operate the website:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Render:</strong> Hosts the Lumi website and application.</li>
        <li><strong>MongoDB Atlas:</strong> Stores account information and user-generated content.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers may process or store information as necessary
        to provide their services. Their own privacy and security
        policies also apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lumi does not sell or rent user information to third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Calendar Time Zone</h2>
      <p>
        Lumi currently interprets calendar dates and scheduled times
        using Bangladesh Standard Time (BST, UTC+6), regardless of
        the user's physical location.
      </p>
      <p>
        Users outside Bangladesh should take this into account
        when scheduling tasks.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        Lumi takes reasonable steps to protect user information,
        including password hashing, authenticated access, and
        security measures designed to prevent unauthorized access.
      </p>
      <p>
        However, no website or method of electronic storage can
        guarantee complete security. Users should keep their
        login credentials confidential and use a strong password.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Account Deletion and Data Removal</h2>
      <p>
        Users can delete their accounts through the account
        settings available on Lumi.
      </p>
      <p>
        When an account is deleted, the associated account
        information and user-generated data, including tasks,
        notes, habits, lessons, and calendar entries, are deleted
        from Lumi's active database.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lumi does not maintain a separate backup database from
        which deleted user data can be restored. We cannot guarantee
        recovery of information after account deletion or data loss.
      </p>
      <p>
        Technical records or copies that may be retained by
        infrastructure providers are subject to those providers'
        own retention practices.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Lumi is not intended for children who are below the
        minimum age at which they can independently consent to
        the processing of their personal information under
        applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you believe a child has provided personal information
        in violation of applicable requirements, please contact
        us so that the matter can be reviewed.
      </p>

      <h2>10. International Users</h2>
      <p>
        Lumi is accessible to users from different countries.
        By using Lumi, you understand that your information may
        be processed or stored in countries where Lumi or its
        infrastructure providers operate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Privacy and data protection laws may differ depending
        on your location.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy when Lumi's features,
        services, or data practices change.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any updates will be published on this page, along with
        a revised effective date. Users are encouraged to review
        this policy periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding
        this Privacy Policy or your personal information,
        contact us at:
      </p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> little.labs16@gmail.com</p>
